23. Dispatch Engine State Machine
IDLE
  ↓
REQUEST_RECEIVED
  ↓
DISCOVER_CANDIDATES
  ↓
FILTER_CANDIDATES
  ↓
CALCULATE_ROUTES
  ↓
CALCULATE_TRAFFIC
  ↓
CALCULATE_SCORES
  ↓
RANK_CANDIDATES
  ↓
SELECT_BEST
  ↓
CREATE_ASSIGNMENT
  ↓
WAIT_FOR_RESPONSE
If accepted:
WAIT_FOR_RESPONSE
       ↓
    ACCEPTED
       ↓
    DISPATCHED
If rejected:
WAIT_FOR_RESPONSE
       ↓
    REJECTED
       ↓
 UPDATE EXCLUSIONS
       ↓
 DISCOVER CANDIDATES
If timeout:
WAIT_FOR_RESPONSE
       ↓
     TIMEOUT
       ↓
 UPDATE EXCLUSIONS
       ↓
 DISCOVER CANDIDATES
________________________________________
24. Real-Time Recalculation
The engine should not assume that the initial conditions remain unchanged.
For example:
10:00

A1 → ETA 8 min
A2 → ETA 10 min
A3 → ETA 12 min
A road suddenly becomes congested:
A1 route → heavy traffic
New calculation:
A1 → ETA 15 min
A2 → ETA 10 min
A3 → ETA 12 min
The system can therefore choose A2 if the dispatch decision has not yet been finalized.
During an active journey, ETA recalculation belongs primarily to the Live Tracking & ETA module, while the dispatch engine is responsible for the initial candidate selection and re-selection when fallback occurs.
