33. 12-Minute Target
The team can use 12 minutes as a target for the simulation, rather than presenting it as an already-proven result.
The experimental process should be:
Target:
≈ 12 minutes

        ↓

Build simulation

        ↓

Run baseline

        ↓

Run UyirKappan

        ↓

Optimize algorithm

        ↓

Run repeated scenarios

        ↓

Measure actual response time
If the simulation achieves:
11.8 minutes
you report the result.
If it achieves:
13.4 minutes
you report that instead and explain the conditions and limitations.
That makes the research much more defensible.
